  "Question": "A square and a triangle have equal perimeters. The lengths of the three sides of the triangle are \\(6.2\\) cm, \\(8.3\\) cm, and \\(9.5\\) cm. The area of the square, in square centimeters, is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(24 \\text{ cm}^2\\)",
    "B": "\\(36 \\text{ cm}^2\\)",
    "C": "\\(48 \\text{ cm}^2\\)",
    "D": "\\(64 \\text{ cm}^2\\)",
    "E": "\\(144 \\text{ cm}^2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "First find the triangle's perimeter, since the square has that same total boundary length:\n\\[\n6.2+8.3+9.5=24\\text{ cm}.\n\\]\nA square has four equal sides, so each side is \\(24\\div4=6\\) cm long. Its area is the side length multiplied by itself:\n\\[\n6\\times6=36\\text{ cm}^2.\n\\]\nThe area is \\(36\\text{ cm}^2\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
